        "structural_family": "ionic salt of a discrete trinuclear [Yb2Er]+ cation bridged by μ2,3-quinolinoxide Hhmq and acetate (Yb···Er about 3.7 Å) with a mononuclear [Er(hfac)3(OAc)(MeOH)]− anion; crystal contains hexane (CCDC: 1.25 C6H14 per ion pair)"
      },
      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Under dry argon using Schlenk technique, Hhmq (3 mmol) and triethylamine (6 mmol) were dissolved in 40 mL of 1:1 H2O/EtOH and stirred at room temperature to a clear yellow solution. Aqueous Yb(OTf)3 (1 mmol in 20 mL) was added dropwise to give a yellow precipitate, which was filtered. The residue and K[Er(hfac)3(OAc)] (3 mmol) were stirred in CH2Cl2 at room temperature for 3 h; addition of 1 mL MeOH cleared the mixture. Yellow crystals were obtained by layering n-hexane on the concentrated CH2Cl2 solution. Yield 65% based on Yb(III). Elemental analysis calcd for C64H45Er2F30N3O25Yb2: C 30.67, H 1.81, N 1.68; found C 30.68, H 1.92, N 1.63. ICP Yb/Er ≈ 1.49:1.55. The main text describes the same sequence without numerical amounts.",
