      },
      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "Compound 1 shows NIR downshifted Yb/Er luminescence and, after addition of fluoride, competitive molecular upconversion under 980 nm excitation at low power density (onset 0.288 W cm−2). With 3.5 equiv [Bu4N]F at 2 W cm−2 and 298 K in non-deuterated solvents, φ_UC (vs ICG, NIR-PMT) reaches 2.29% in toluene; the paper also states 2.78% by NIR-PMT and at least a 20-fold improvement over earlier molecular examples. Yb(III)→Er(III) energy transfer is more efficient than ligand→Er transfer.",
        "measurements": [
